 "summary": "Mathlib's SelbergSieve stops at the quadratic-form diagonalisation and has no truncated normaliser, Selberg weights or M\u00f6bius upper-divisor sum, and Tau Ceti has no prior copy of any of them. The PR builds on the existing Mathlib results (restricted M\u00f6bius inversion, divisors_filter_dvd_of_dvd, mainSum_lambdaSquared_eq_sum_mul_sum_sq, upperMoebius_lambdaSquared, siftedSum_le_mainSum_errSum_of_upperMoebius) rather than re-deriving them.",
